There IS, and has always been. For example:
nethack -s 100
will show you the 100 top scores, which usually means the whole record
list. Replace 100 with a smaller number to get less scores.

I also wrote a couple of years ago a utility called reclist that gives a
little bit more information and has some more selection options than
nethack -s. You can find it at http://www.netsonic.fi/~walker/nethack.html

